<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila SEC set to revoke futures exchange licence.</title>
<headline>Manila SEC set to revoke futures exchange licence.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) said on Thursday it will revoke the licence of the Manila International Futures Exchange before the year ends if the bourse fails to submit its reform programme.</p>
<p>&quot;There is no use for us to delay. We have given MIFE ample time,&quot; SEC chairman Perfecto Yasay said at a news conference.</p>
<p>The SEC suspended the operations of MIFE on June 20 due to complaints from the public of widespread irregularities.</p>
<p>But MIFE officials said they would come up with reforms to reform the industry.</p>
<p>--Manila newsroom (632) 841-89-36, fax 817-62-67</p>
